  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the point dividing te line segment in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, then<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0054_2b31d1666e87.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.67361in;height:0.33333in\" /><br /><math><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math> and <math><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Locus of <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>, which is a circle.</p><p>Hence, the perimeter of the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>&nbsp;units</p>"
  }
